  "query_preview": "..A cut off low will move into Arizona today and then \nslowly move towards the north on Sunday. This will keep it cool \nacross northern Arizona through the weekend. Moisture has been slow \nto exit the region and as a result we will continue to see some \nscattered showers and thunderstorms into this evening across the \nregion. As the low lifts to the north on Sunday, the best chance for \nany additional showers will towards the Four Corners region. \nRainfall amounts look to be light but with the already wet \nconditions, some areas may see some localized flooding.\n\nHeading into Monday, the flow becomes more zonal with a trough \npassing well to the north of our area. Temperatures are expected to \nwarm with drier air pushing into the region. This pattern looks to \nhold through about midweek, when the next trough starts to dig down \nfrom the Pacific Northwest. Guidance shows moisture increasing as \nsub-tropical moisture is pulled toward the region in the developing \nsouthwest flow as early as Thursday, with chances for showers and \nthunderstorms returning to end the week.",
